From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:11:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: hand the console back on a VT switch

A desktop on a tty holds DRM master for as long as it runs, and Ctrl+Alt+F2
does not take it away. So switching to another VT left two owners on one CRTC:
the kernel drawing a console it believed it had, and Chromium still scanning
out over it. There was nothing to do about it from inside the desktop, and the
way back was a reboot or an ssh session.

THE SEAMS WERE ALL THERE AND UNGATED. NativeDisplayDelegate::
RelinquishDisplayControl reaches DrmWrapper::DropMaster through
DrmDisplayHostManager and the DRM thread, and TakeDisplayControl reaches
SetMaster the same way. What did not exist off ChromeOS is a caller, because on
ChromeOS the session manager owns the VT and ash never asks. This is that
caller: VT_SETMODE in VT_PROCESS mode, a handler per signal, and the handshake
the kernel expects.

TESTED WHERE THE ORDER IS. `StepVtSwitch` is a free function for the reason
`ModesetParamsFromSnapshots` is one: a tty, two signals, a self-pipe and an
asynchronous delegate are wiring that only a real console exercises, while the
ORDER of the handshake is where a mistake costs somebody their screen. Eleven
cases, written first, and the two that carry a decision were watched failing
against a table that got them wrong:

A relinquish that FAILS refuses the switch. console_ioctl(2) allows a process
to answer VT_RELDISP with 0, and this is what that is for -- acknowledging a
switch we could not release the display for hands the console to the kernel
while Chromium is still scanning out on it, which is the two-owner bug this
patch exists to remove, arriving by the other door.

A take that fails acknowledges anyway and remembers that it did.  An acqsig
cannot be refused: by the time it arrives the console is already ours. But
going back to "owned" would be a lie, and the next switch away would try to
relinquish a display we do not have, fail, and refuse -- stranding somebody on
a console nothing can paint. `kConsoleWithoutDisplay` is that state and its
only job is that the way out stays open.

Two smaller things the compiler would not have caught. The signal handler
writes one byte to a pipe and the message loop does everything else, because
`write` is async-signal-safe and a delegate call, a log line and an ioctl are
not. And the destructor restores VT_AUTO: a VT left in VT_PROCESS waits on a
handshake from a process that is exiting.

WHAT THIS IS NOT is a recovery mechanism, and it is worth being plain because
it is the first thing it will be asked for. The handshake runs in this process,
so a browser wedged in a GPU wait never answers relsig and the kernel refuses
the switch. A browser that dies needs none of this -- the kernel drops master
when the fd closes and switches anyway. This makes a working desktop usable.

Input is the other half and is not here: until the evdev fds are revoked on the
same two edges, keys typed at another VT still reach this one.
---
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn              |  3 ++
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn
index 1d789a5ce9f5..50dc4586f2a7 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn
@@ -124,6 +124,8 @@ source_set("gbm") {
     "domicile/drm_modeset.h",
     "domicile/drm_screen.cc",
     "domicile/drm_screen.h",
+    "domicile/drm_vt_switcher.cc",
+    "domicile/drm_vt_switcher.h",
     "host/drm_window_host_manager.h",
     "host/gpu_thread_adapter.h",
     "host/gpu_thread_observer.h",
@@ -236,6 +238,7 @@ source_set("gbm_unittests") {
     "gpu/proxy_helpers_unittest.cc",
     "domicile/drm_modeset_unittest.cc",
     "domicile/drm_screen_unittest.cc",
+    "domicile/drm_vt_switcher_unittest.cc",
   ]
 
   # `ui/display/manager/test/fake_display_snapshot.h` is the one thing this
diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc
index 3fd2c99b3bae..3c23bee3cf3e 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.h"
 
+#include <fcntl.h>
 #include <gbm.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <xf86drm.h>
@@ -14,9 +15,12 @@
 #include "base/check.h"
 #include "base/command_line.h"
 #include "base/containers/flat_set.h"
+#include "base/files/scoped_file.h"
 #include "base/functional/bind.h"
+#include "base/logging.h"
 #include "base/memory/weak_ptr.h"
 #include "base/notreached.h"
+#include "base/posix/eintr_wrapper.h"
 #include "base/task/single_thread_task_runner.h"
 #include "base/threading/platform_thread.h"
 #include "build/build_config.h"
@@ -48,6 +52,7 @@
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h"
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/domicile/drm_modeset.h"
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/domicile/drm_screen.h"
+#include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/domicile/drm_vt_switcher.h"
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host_manager.h"
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/host_drm_device.h"
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/mojom/drm_device.mojom.h"
@@ -110,6 +115,31 @@ class OzonePlatformDrm : public OzonePlatform {
     modeset_ = std::make_unique<DrmModeset>(CreateNativeDisplayDelegate(),
                                             static_cast<DrmScreen*>(screen));
     modeset_->Start();
+
+    // And the console this is running on, so Ctrl+Alt+F<n> hands the display
+    // back instead of leaving two owners on one CRTC.
+    //
+    // `/dev/tty` and not `/dev/tty0`: the first is this process's controlling
+    // terminal, which is the VT the desktop was started from, and the second
+    // is whichever VT is active at the moment it is opened. Asking the wrong
+    // one to raise signals at us is how a handshake ends up installed on
+    // somebody else's console.
+    //
+    // FAILING IS ORDINARY AND IS NOT FATAL. A desktop nested in a Wayland
+    // session has no VT, a service started without a controlling terminal has
+    // no `/dev/tty`, and neither should stop a browser from starting. What is
+    // lost is only the ability to switch away, which is what the log line
+    // says.
+    base::ScopedFD tty(HANDLE_EINTR(open("/dev/tty", O_RDWR | O_CLOEXEC)));
+    if (!tty.is_valid()) {
+      VPLOG(1) << "no controlling terminal, so no VT switching";
+      return;
+    }
+    auto switcher = std::make_unique<DrmVtSwitcher>(
+        CreateNativeDisplayDelegate(), std::move(tty));
+    if (switcher->Start()) {
+      vt_switcher_ = std::move(switcher);
+    }
   }
 
   GpuPlatformSupportHost* GetGpuPlatformSupportHost() override {
@@ -395,6 +425,7 @@ class OzonePlatformDrm : public OzonePlatform {
   // after display_manager_ so it is destroyed before the manager whose
   // delegate it holds.
   std::unique_ptr<DrmModeset> modeset_;
+  std::unique_ptr<DrmVtSwitcher> vt_switcher_;
   PlatformRuntimeProperties host_properties_;
 
   base::WeakPtrFactory<OzonePlatformDrm> weak_factory_{this};
